// The inverse of `loader`: a `model` workbook back into the document tree the
// `yaml` seam writes. Pure — no filesystem, no Excel backend — so it tests on
// values alone, like the rest of the compiler core (ADR-003).
//
// This is where the *names* are invented. The file a spec compiled to kept every
// bit of sharing and lost every name (ADR-017), so a style used on forty cells
// arrives here as one style and no word for it; naming it is the last thing
// between a recovered spec and one somebody would keep.
import {
  "t-ujiie-g/yxl/model",
  "t-ujiie-g/yxl/units",
  "t-ujiie-g/yxl/yaml",
  // Sets of the addresses and names already spoken for.
  "moonbitlang/core/set",
}
